## 2. Separate Input and Output Schemas (`CT2`)

Never share a single class across request and response, and never serialize an ORM/persistence model or internal domain entity directly on the wire:

| Direction | Naming & Validation Contract | Project Pattern |
|---|---|---|
| **Create Input (`POST`)** | `<Resource>CreateRequest` — strict input validation (`{{strict_input_config}}`), explicit bounds on strings/collections/numbers; excludes server-generated `id`, `created_at`, `tenant_id`, and privileged role/status flags. | `{{create_schema_example}}` |
| **Patch Input (`PATCH`)** | `<Resource>UpdateRequest` — only mutable fields, all optional with explicit partial-update semantics (`exclude_unset=True` or equivalent), strict unknown-field rejection (`{{strict_input_config}}`). | `{{update_schema_example}}` |
| **Output (`200`/`201`)** | `<Resource>Response` / `<Resource>SummaryResponse` — explicit public projection; excludes password hashes, secret tokens, internal audit columns, and raw foreign-key join tables. | `{{response_schema_example}}` |

