## 3. Single Structured Error Envelope & Status Codes (`CT3`, `CT4`)

All `4xx` and `5xx` responses across the service — including framework validation errors (`422`), authentication failures (`401`), permission denials (`403`), and unhandled exceptions (`500`) — must return the project's single structured error envelope (`{{error_envelope_model}}` at `{{error_envelope_path}}`):

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "Work order was not found.",
    "details": [
      { "field": "work_order_id", "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "No record matches the supplied identifier." }
    ],
    "trace_id": "01J8Z9X4K2M3N4P5Q6R7S8T9U0"
  }
}
```

### Status Code Decision Table (`CT4`)

| Status | Meaning | Required Contract Declaration |
|---|---|---|
| `200 OK` | Synchronous read (`GET`) or state transition returning updated resource | Explicit `<Resource>Response` or `Page[<Resource>SummaryResponse]` |
| `201 Created` | Resource created (`POST`) | Explicit `<Resource>Response` + `Location` header when applicable |
| `202 Accepted` | Asynchronous job accepted | Explicit `JobAcceptedResponse` (`job_id`, `status_url`) |
| `204 No Content` | Delete or void command with empty body | Explicit empty response body (`status_code=204`) |
| `400 Bad Request` | Malformed syntax or unparseable query/header | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`BAD_REQUEST`) |
| `401 Unauthorized` | Missing, expired, or invalid authentication credential | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`UNAUTHENTICATED`) + `WWW-Authenticate` |
| `403 Forbidden` | Authenticated principal lacks required role/scope (`CT5`) | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`PERMISSION_DENIED`) |
| `404 Not Found` | Resource does not exist **or** belongs to another tenant/owner (`CT5` anti-IDOR) | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND`) |
| `409 Conflict` | Business state conflict, optimistic lock version mismatch, or duplicate `Idempotency-Key` with mismatched payload | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`CONFLICT` / `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT`) |
| `422 Unprocessable Entity` | Request DTO/field validation failure | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` with `details[].field`) |
| `429 Too Many Requests` | Rate limit or quota exceeded | `{{error_envelope_model}}` (`RATE_LIMITED`) + `Retry-After` header |

